From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Burr <christopher.burr@cern.ch>
Date: Tue, 3 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix cross-compilation with CMake >= 4.1 (CMP0190)

CMake 4.1 introduced policy CMP0190 which makes FindPython search target
artifacts and require CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR when the Interpreter
component is requested alongside Development. conda-forge cross builds use
crossenv (a host-runnable interpreter, no emulator), so restore the
previous behaviour. Same approach as the gdal and freud feedstocks.
---
diff --git a/python/CMakeLists.txt b/python/CMakeLists.txt
index c32bea2..4fe491a 100644
--- a/python/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/python/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -2,6 +2,18 @@ cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.18...4.1 FATAL_ERROR)
 
 project(PyXRootD LANGUAGES CXX)
 
+# CMake >= 4.1 (policy CMP0190) makes FindPython search *target* artifacts and
+# require CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR whenever the Interpreter component is
+# requested alongside Development. conda-forge cross builds use crossenv, which
+# provides a host-runnable interpreter (no emulator), so restore the previous
+# behaviour. Same workaround as the gdal and freud feedstocks, but guarded so it
+# is a no-op on CMake < 4.1. Must live here, not in the top-level CMakeLists.txt:
+# this file's own cmake_minimum_required(...4.1) resets the policy to NEW for the
+# subdirectory scope, overriding any setting inherited from the parent.
+if(POLICY CMP0190)
+  cmake_policy(SET CMP0190 OLD)
+endif()
+
 find_package(Python REQUIRED COMPONENTS Interpreter Development.Module)
 
 if(CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR STREQUAL PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR OR PYPI_BUILD)
-- 
